<title>TURKEY: Two-way traffic resumes on Bosphorus Strait.</title>
<headline>Two-way traffic resumes on Bosphorus Strait.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bosphorus Strait was reopened to two-way crossing as fog lifted on Tuesday morning, maritime officials said.</p>
<p>Northbound traffic was stopped at 0300 GMT due to dense fog, and only passenger ships less than 100 metres (yards) were allowed to sail southbound.</p>
<p>Officials said northbound traffic resumed at 1100 local time (0900 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +0212 2750875</p>
</text>
